You can't charge them with that. So then late last&nbsp;
week, a three judge panel voted 2 to 1 that, yeah,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.140 --> 00:01:41.700
yeah, you can charge these individuals with&nbsp;
obstructing an official congressional proceeding.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.360 --> 00:01:47.640
Now, what's important about that, according to&nbsp;
former Assistant Manhattan District Attorney&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.640 --> 00:01:57.060
