judge panel ruling 2 to 1 vote and basically come&nbsp;
to the decision. We don't want to wade into this.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.540 --> 00:03:46.980
If they come to that decision, they will say,&nbsp;
nope, we are not taking the case. The D.C.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.980 --> 00:03:52.680
Circuit's decision stand. That clears the way for&nbsp;
Jack Smith, of course, to hit Trump with these&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:52.680 --> 00:03:58.200
obstruction charges if they choose to take it up.&nbsp;
God only knows how that's going to end up. Right.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:58.200 --> 00:04:05.400
We have seen this court. Absolutely. Railroad&nbsp;
legal precedent. We don't know. So there's a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:05.400 --> 00:04:10.680
big question mark over that. So 5050 chance they&nbsp;
take it up, then? If they take it up, 5050 chance&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:10.680 --> 00:04:16.620
there that they rule that, yes, you can charge&nbsp;
these individuals. So let's assume for a moment&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:17.220 --> 00:04:22.920
that Jack Smith gets the clearance. The Supreme&nbsp;
Court either doesn't take it up or rules in favor&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:22.920 --> 00:04:30.960
of the D.C. Circuit, and Smith can charge Donald&nbsp;
Trump with obstruction of an official proceeding.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:32.280 --> 00:04:37.620
That's a relatively minor charge compared to,&nbsp;
obviously, everything else that Jack Smith&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:37.620 --> 00:04:45.060
is investigating. So if Smith moves forward and&nbsp;
decides to charge Donald Trump with obstruction,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:45.060 --> 00:04:52.080
it's going to be a very minor charge on top of&nbsp;
everything else that he could potentially be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:52.080 --> 00:04:57.180
charging him with. So it's basically a way to&nbsp;
just kind of pad everything a little bit more.&nbsp;&nbsp;

