Because to me, what I'm reading into this.&nbsp;
Is that if you can charge any of these people&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:12.180 --> 00:05:18.600
involved in the events of January 6th with&nbsp;
obstructing an official government proceeding.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:19.560 --> 00:05:26.700
That is something that Jack Smith can then use as&nbsp;
a bargaining chip against any of the individuals&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:26.700 --> 00:05:32.640
who may not want to cooperate fully with the&nbsp;
investigation. Maybe we want to plead the Fifth.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:32.640 --> 00:05:37.740
Maybe we we don't want to come talk to you. Maybe&nbsp;
we want to challenge these subpoenas. Of course,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:37.740 --> 00:05:43.560
we've seen all this happen so far, to no avail&nbsp;
on the part of most of the people that have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:43.560 --> 00:05:50.160
been subpoenaed. But this would give Jack Smith a&nbsp;
really great bargaining chip because it's a fairly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:50.160 --> 00:05:56.280
simple and easy charge to prove. And it's also&nbsp;
something that most prosecutors would not want to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:56.280 --> 00:06:04.200
